{"from": "artifact:4q174-florilegium", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:jn-12-34-christ-remains-forever", "grade": "C", "note": "A pre-Christian (Herodian-period) Qumran midrash, a 'Midrash on the Last Days', quotes 2 Samuel 7:10-14 - the eternal-throne promise - with eschatological commentary: the expectation that the Christ remains forever existed in Judea before this crowd. It attests the expectation, not the crowd's words. Regraded B to C by architect review, consistent with Psalms of Solomon 17 and 4Q521: a pre-Christian messianic expectation is context for what a crowd said."}
{"from": "site:bethany-al-eizariya", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:jn-12-02-supper-martha-served", "grade": "C", "note": "The excavated village of Bethany (al-Eizariya; Saller 1949-1953: houses, wine-presses, cisterns and silos, Persian-to-Roman pottery) confirms the supper's setting village (reused node and sources; the exact ancient site is disputed)."}
{"from": "text:mishnah-sukkah-4-5", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:jn-12-13-hosanna-king-of-israel", "grade": "C", "note": "The Mishnah records pilgrims circling the altar crying 'Lord, please save us!' (ana Adonai hoshia-na, the origin of 'Hosanna') with branches in hand - the same acclamation-word in Temple festival liturgy, though at Tabernacles; redacted c. 200 CE, so it may not describe the practice of the 30s CE exactly."}
